{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792445841,"nonce":"8p5t0a4H3u3XbJ9kbANiD2tR9u4=","message":"Final Unsupported audit against blinc_abi a92f5c0, schema 1 and 112-float records:\n\n- Kind: the producer emits only rect 0, shadow 3, text 7, image 32, canvas 33, layer-begin 40, layer 41 and backdrop 42. plan() handles each. Primitive-only decode()/Record::primitive deliberately report the ordered-pass kinds; consumers must use plan() and Painter for a whole scene. Unknown kinds and unbalanced layers remain reported. An invalid/unclosed layer is drawn flat and named; invalid individual records are omitted and named.\n- Gradient: the producer uses solid/linear/radial/conic fills 0/1/2/3. Multi-stop and repeating tables are carried into aux rows. The remaining Gradient error is for an unknown fill or missing/empty table. GradientTable is a limit of Record::to_primitive without caller-owned aux/list data; Record::primitive/decode/plan carry those tables.\n- ClipShape: producer element-frame shapes are none/ellipse/rounded-rect/polygon 0/1/2/3 and all are drawn, including multi-ring nonzero/even-odd paths. Remaining errors indicate invalid/absent point rows, or use of to_primitive/image without the required list/aux payload. Their aux-aware forms and plan handle valid geometry.\n- Notch: producer notch assignments occur only on boxes, their shadows and backdrops, all implemented. Other-kind notch data is rejected.\n- Degenerate: zero/near-singular affine determinants (at or below 1e-12, or NaN) deliberately omit the record to avoid unstable inverse transforms. This remains a reported transparent fallback, including very small valid numerical transforms; it is not a new feature gap.\n- GlyphMode: valid producer modes 0, 1 and 2 are drawn. Other selectors are invalid.\n- ImageMapping: producer fit values 0 through 5 and repeat axes 0 through 3 are handled, including background brushes. The producer mapping setter rejects unknown fits/nonfinite positions. Bad resource intrinsic geometry and missing image slots remain caller-owned resolution failures, returned as missing slots. SDK slot encodings stay the caller's concern.\n- CanvasData: resource slots are limited by the producer setter to 0..16777215, matching the reader. Nonfinite/invalid geometry or scale is rejected. Registered callbacks draw valid slots; absent callbacks are intentionally omitted and reported through missing_canvases rather than Plan::unsupported.\n- BackdropEffect: Gaussian deviations/read margins must be finite and nonnegative. Valid backdrops and glass effects are implemented, with an independent oracle. Invalid values stay rejected.\n- LayerEffect: the last valid-producer feature rejection, masks beyond 16 stops, is removed by this slice. Real tables through 4099 stops are exercised. Only invalid kinds/spreads/indices/counts/stop values or table ranges remain rejected. Invalid effects draw their content flat and are named. Normal GPU resource/texture dimension/allocation limits still apply.\n\nThere is no remaining valid-producer feature reported unsupported by plan(). The conservative Degenerate fallback and missing consumer resources above are deliberate and documented. The source audit is backed by the decoder suite, the full offscreen display-list suite, and the per-slice encoder fixtures/oracles and mutation evidence linked in fa2406c. Native 3D SDF, particles, meshes and other features with no ABI records remain on the native path.\n\nSeparate work stays open: ce34b2083b4e5cfa939b7b8ef94055fc4f5782019afe5effd3d11e612693dd50 for stale primitive DT/WebGL2 packing; 178a63be19ea1c0a8e220f4e48ff58337276009f5cca2c939e0271d3782604b6 for shared ClipPath Polygon/Path and CSS keyword ownership, pending the owner and ashui. The ABI fill-rule bit and native DrawContext fill-rule plumbing are already covered; no shared enum or CSS keyword changes were made here. Broader blur/mobile performance followups and the DSL migration decision remain outside this catch-up task. Actual WebGL2 and PowerVR/Adreno/mobile pixels are unverified.\n\nAfter the final feature commit and gate results are recorded, fa2406c meets HANDOFF.md's stated completion criterion: every valid producer Unsupported case is drawn or has a documented fallback. The handoff then authorizes deleting the untracked handoff file. No code or tracker data will be pushed without an explicit request.","files":null}]}